			"date": "2023-08-25T07:43:13.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@ascorbic\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>ascorbic</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Sure, that was the whole point of <a href=\"https://github.com/gatsbyjs/gatsby/discussions/36608\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">github.com/gatsbyjs/gatsby/dis</span><span class=\"invisible\">cussions/36608</span></a> - achieving island architecture and doing *something* different with RSC than Next (e.g. with a data layer in the cloud). See the comments from Dan and Ward at the bottom</p>",
