			"date": "2023-08-25T07:51:24.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@lekoarts\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>lekoarts</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> OK, but as Ward says in there the goal wasn't really to implement RSC - it was to find a solution to support partial hydration. Do you think Gatsby needs full RSC support, or just fix the current implementation?</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
