			"date": "2023-08-25T08:02:37.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@ascorbic\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>ascorbic</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Ok, sorry, my answer was a bit vague. I meant: Implement RSC (but not fully) in a way that makes most sense for Gatsby to e.g. achieve island architecture and possible other improvements (innovation needed here). So short term make Partial Hydration production-ready.</p>",
